---
Implement 3-band parametric EQ effect.

Three configurable bands (low/mid/high) with frequency, gain, and Q.
Most important mixing tool after the compressor.

## Parameters (per band × 3)
- frequency: Center frequency (20-20000 Hz)
- gain: Boost/cut in dB (-12 to +12)
- q: Bandwidth / Q factor (0.1-10)
- type: Low shelf / Peaking / High shelf

## Implementation
- 3 cascaded biquad filters
- Robert Bristow-Johnson's Audio EQ Cookbook formulae
- Smooth parameter interpolation to avoid clicks

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] EFFECT_EQ added to effect type enum
- [ ] 3 independently configurable bands
- [ ] Shelf and peaking modes per band
- [ ] No audible artifacts during parameter sweeps
- [ ] Flat response when all gains = 0 dB

## Test Plan
- [ ] Boost 1kHz by 12dB, verify on exported WAV
- [ ] Cut bass with low shelf, verify audible change
- [ ] All-flat = bit-perfect passthrough
